title: Show the player something
intro: Camera Controls can take the camera over for a while: it glides to a character, follows it closer in, then hands the camera back.

project: Empty | Camera Focus

chapter: A level, a camera and a walker | Camera Controls on the camera
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Walker
set: Transform.Position = 10, -4, 0
add: Mover
set: Mover.Speed = 1.5
say: The walker paces back and forth across the level by itself.
deselect
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Size = 9
set: Camera.HudSize = 9
add: CameraControls
pick: CameraControls.StayInside = Level
set: CameraControls.FocusSize = 3
explain: field:CameraControls.FocusSize | Focus Size | Focus Size is how close the camera zooms in while it's focused on something. Focus Seconds is how long it takes to glide there, and to zoom back out.

chapter: A button that shows the walker | Focus On, by name
deselect
create: Button
rename: Show Walker
set: Button.Action = Do
pick: Button.Targets = Main Camera
pick: Button.Do = Focus On
set: Button.With = Walker
set: Button.Shortcut = F
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 2.5, -1.5
explain: field:Button.Do | Do | Camera Controls can do Focus On, with the name of what to follow, and Release. A trigger can do them too, so a guided tour needs no code.
deselect
create: Button
rename: Back
set: Button.Action = Do
pick: Button.Targets = Main Camera
pick: Button.Do = Release
set: Button.Shortcut = R
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 2.5, -3

chapter: Play | It follows, then hands back
play
wait: 1
hold: Right 1
say: The player pans as usual.
tap: F
wait: 1.5
say: F clicks Show Walker. The camera glides over to the walker, zooming in, and follows it as it paces.
hold: Left 1
wheel: game = down 3
expectvalue: Main Camera.CameraControls.IsFocused = true
say: Meanwhile the keys and the wheel wait. The camera is the game's for now.
tap: R
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Main Camera.CameraControls.IsFocused = false
expectvalue: Main Camera.Camera.Size = 9
say: R clicks Back. The camera zooms back out to where it was, and hands control back right where it is.
hold: Right 1
wheel: game = up 2
say: The keys pan and the wheel zooms again.
stop
